o"><country>JP</country><doc-number>61190936</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9146283-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9146283</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1119028A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURAMOCHI SATORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIMURA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADIKA NOZOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>USHIO ELECTRIC INC</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAMOCHI, SATORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIMURA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADIKA, NOZOMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>USHIO DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURAMOCHI SATORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIMURA YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADIKA NOZOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAMOCHI, SATORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIMURA, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADIKA, NOZOMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A silicon wafer coated with resist, while being heated and cooled, is attracted on a work stage by suction and irradiated with ultraviolet rays to cure the resist without causing scratches on the back of the silicon wafer. An apparatus for curing resist comprises a source of ultraviolet rays, and a work stage (10) including means for holding a silicon wafer by suction and means for controlling the temperature of the silicon wafer. Ultraviolet rays cure the resist while the resist-coated silicon wafer held on the work stage is heated. The ultraviolet irradiation is carried out with a plate (60) interposed airtightly between the work stage and the silicon wafer. The plate (60) consists of any of Si, SiO2, SiC and Si3N4.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une plaquette de silicium recouverte de résist qui, lors de son chauffage et de son refroidissement, est retenue sur un plateau de travail par succion puis soumise à une irradiation par rayons ultraviolets, ce qui permet de durcir le résist sans provoquer de rayures à l'arrière de la plaque de silicium. Un appareil de durcissement de résist comprend une source de rayons ultraviolets et un plateau (10) de travail comprenant un organe de retenue d'une plaquette de silicium par succion et un organe de commande de la température de la plaquette de silicium. Les rayons ultraviolets durcissent le résist pendant que la plaquette de silicium recouverte de résist retenue sur le plateau de travail est chauffée. L'irradiation par rayons ultraviolets s'effectue à l'aide d'une plaque (60) intercalée de façon totalement étanche entre le plateau de travail et la plaquette de silicium. La plaque (60) est formée de Si, SiO2, SiC ou Si3N4.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>